<!-- f16-resident readout, gemma4-12b F16, RK1, 600 MHz, 2026-09-01.
     One warm-up-sized process per arm (-p 512 -n 0 -r 1), ROCKET_LOG_STDERR=1, stderr kept,
     drop_caches between arms. Generator: perf/data/f16-resident-readout.sh.
     STOCK RESIDENTS ZERO: no [f16-resident] line at all, which by that line's own condition
     means nothing was offered to the route -- this model's K is above the default prepack
     gate. That is what makes the pinning campaign's arms the STREAMED configuration.
     THE KNOB REACHES 87%, and admission stops at the NPU IOVA window rather than at the
     21127 MB budget, so 'a 12B F16 cannot be held resident on this board' is retired.
-->
== gemma4-12b-f16 ==
  stock:
  ROCKET_F16_RESIDENT=auto:
    [f16-resident] weights offered to the resident route: 286 resident on the NPU (18078MB), 42 streamed via the per-call pack -- 87% resident
    [f16-resident] admission first declined at 18078MB resident: the NPU IOVA window filled (raise ROCKET_N_THREADS for more fds)

stderr kept under <data>/f16-resident-readout

